{
  "name": "the shapes, edge by edge",
  "why": "Every edge a trapezoid has, asked at its corners and halfway along its slopes: a triangle written with three points, a trapezoid, a shoulder whose rise is vertical, and one on the far edge of the range. The sets leave a gap between 7 and 8 on purpose, so one case can ask a rule base with a hole in it what it concludes -- and the answer is null, not a number that looks like one.",
